# Normalize line endings so the mirror's object database stays LF regardless of
# the platform that ran the publish. Without this the assembled tree is copied
# straight from a Windows working directory and every source file lands in the
# repo as CRLF, showing up as a whole-repo diff on the first publish.
* text=auto

# Generated data — check out as LF on every platform, not just where the shell
# happens to be POSIX.
#
# `npm run generate` writes '\n' unconditionally. Under plain `text=auto` with
# `core.autocrlf=true` git hands Windows a CRLF checkout, the next regeneration
# rewrites it as LF, and these five files then sit in `git status` as permanently
# modified — while `git diff` shows nothing, because the content is identical once
# normalized. That combination is worse than either failure alone: the tree looks
# dirty, so a real drift in the generated data is easy to wave away as "just the
# line-ending thing", and the CI drift gate is the only honest reading left.
Sources/VinodexCore/Resources/*.json text eol=lf

# Known binary types — explicit so git's content-sniffing heuristic never
# mis-detects them (matters most for the rasterized Icons/ and Flags/ trees and
# the pixelflags/ source).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
